From e24aedd841f772672e99da22f7c74f763ef675bb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ken5998 <46025606+Ken5998@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 15:54:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 20/21] perf(apu): run the DSP interpreter's hot paths inline

The GP DSP runs a fixed effect chain of about 24,000 instructions a frame and
took 610-720 us of the 667 us audio frame on the RP6, so sound fell behind.
On a frame captured on the device it now needs 1.4x fewer host instructions,
with the final DSP state byte-identical to before:

- instructions run in batches while no DMA transfer, wait or stop needs a
  look between them, instead of one call and five checks each
- X and Y RAM and mix buffer accesses, plain register writes and linear
  address updates take inline fast paths; the full paths are unchanged
- the parallel-move helpers, effective-address decode and PC update inline
- a bare move skips the empty ALU call, and REP repeats reuse the decoded
  opcode while P memory still holds the fetched word
---
